    {
      "body": "Not stale — just re-verified against current `main`: the cascade branch in `TritonAttentionMetadataBuilder.build` still never assigns `prefix_scheduler_metadata` (only the `else` branch does, [triton_attn.py#L211-L226](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/vllm/v1/attention/backends/triton_attn.py#L211-L226)), so any `common_prefix_len > 0` build still hits the UnboundLocalError. The branch is conflict-free against main and includes a regression test for the cascade path.\n\n@tjtanaa @gshtras would appreciate a look when you get a chance — it's a two-line fix.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-07-19T14:41:21Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/39208#issuecomment-5016130852",
      "id": 5016130852,
      "updated_at": "2026-07-19T14:41:21Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "Bortlesboat"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Closing as obsolete: merged #61126 removed cascade attention, including this builder's `use_cascade` branch and the `prefix_scheduler_metadata` field/argument, in e1a5086256a00c47a968aac6a583c25d040100a7. I checked the removal diff and current main; the unbound-local path addressed here no longer exists. There is no useful rebase of this patch onto the replacement builder. The original MI300X regression evidence remains historical.\r\n",
